37:The token-savings figures above come from single, focused comprehension tasks where the agent used aptu-coder instead of shell search. Agentic coding loops have bash and ripgrep and can search the repo directly. The [v19 benchmark program](https://github.com/clouatre-labs/aptu-coder/blob/main/docs/audit/2026-09-30-v19-pivot.md) (N=20 paired sessions, pre-registered claim gate) measured aptu-coder in those loops: no measurable answer-quality gain over bash + ripgrep on structural fan-in tasks (pooled paired F1 diff mean -0.071, 95% CI [-0.179, +0.038]; gate NOT-SUPPORTED); tool activation itself was reliable when tools were surfaced directly. Recommended uses: premise grounding for multi-agent workflows, and non-agentic MCP consumers (IDE assistants, CI jobs, scoring pipelines).
47:aptu-coder is a comprehension layer for coding agents: it gives an agent harness precise structural context about a codebase, directory trees, and symbol definitions, without the agent reading raw files or re-deriving structure on every call. That prevents context starvation on large or unfamiliar codebases while keeping the result set small enough to fit the model's context window. It supports 18 languages (see [Supported Languages](#supported-languages)) and integrates with any MCP-compatible orchestrator.
